WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.674
Cardinality describes how many rows can match a key
A one-to-one

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.568
join is simple because each key can match at most
once on

00:00:08.595 --> 00:00:14.745
both sides In a one-to-many join one patient can
match several admissions

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:20.524
The patient row repeats once for each matching
admission That is normal

00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:25.691
and often exactly what we want The danger appears
when we join

00:00:25.718 --> 00:00:29.494
several one-to-many child tables at the same time
using only the parent

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.470
key Suppose one patient has two admissions two lab
tests and two

00:00:34.497 --> 00:00:39.352
prescriptions The join can create two times two
times two or eight

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:45.832
combinations Those eight rows are not eight new
business events They

00:00:45.858 --> 00:00:51.385
are combinations of existing detail rows Before you
aggregate a

00:00:51.412 --> 00:00:56.677
multi-table join predict this behavior If your
target output is one row

00:00:56.691 --> 00:01:00.875
per patient consider summarizing each child table to
patient grain first
